        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ریزگرد",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ریزگرد (rizgard) — \"fine dust (in the air), dust haze\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "به خاطر ریزگرد مدرسه ها تعطیل شدند. Be khâter-e rizgard madrese-hâ ta'til shodand. Because of the dust haze the schools closed."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Dust from the deserts is a serious problem in the west and south of the country."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "rizgard is a modern native compound of riz 'fine, tiny' and gard 'dust', which EtymDB lists."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
