              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "مه آلود (mehâlud) — \"foggy, misty\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "صبح جاده مه آلود بود و آهسته رانندگی کردیم. Sobh jâdde mehâlud bud va âheste rânandegi kardim. In the morning the road was foggy and we drove slowly."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "meh 'fog' + âlud 'covered with', from âludan."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "mehâlud is a native compound of inherited words: meh 'fog', usually traced to Middle Persian mēgh, and âlud 'covered, smeared', the past stem of âludan 'to soil, to smear', as in âlude 'polluted'."
            }
          ]
        },
